  "recommended_range": [380000.00, 425747.50],
  "walk_away": 377747.50,
  "reasoning": "All figures base date Oct. 24, 2026. The four deemed-accepted invoices accrue $2,652.00/month (1%/month under Section 2 on $265,200.00; approx. $87.19/day) until paid, so every number below drifts upward with delay. Record-supported band. Floor $377,747.50 = $265,200.00 (J-4411 $68,400 + J-4452 $71,250 + J-4490 $66,100 + J-4571 $59,450; Section 2 deemed-accepted - no dispute within 15 days - and Pinecrest's own Sept. 29 counsel letter calls them 'undisputed') + $8,847.50 accrued interest (J-4411 5 mo x $684.00 = $3,420.00; J-4452 4 x $712.50 = $2,850.00; J-4490 3 x $661.00 = $1,983.00; J-4571 1 x $594.50 = $594.50) + $32,000.00 conversion fees for Anne O./Victor H. (2 x 25% x $64,000.00 assumed comp; the only written Section 3 waiver, the Feb. 11 Bell email, covers Rosa M./Tay W. only, and the file shows no contact at all about the June hires) + $71,700.00 J-4533 net (invoice $74,800.00 less our $3,100.00 credit for the two double-entered shifts the client admits). Ceiling $425,747.50 = same with the full five-worker fee block at $80,000.00 (5 x $16,000.00). The $64,000.00 average-comp assumption is unverified in both directions. Recommended range $380,000.00-$425,747.50: lower end is the rounded corridor; expected-value midpoint is $401,747.50 = $377,747.50 + 50% x $48,000.00 (the Priya S./Luis F./Keisha B. implied-waiver fight - Apr. 22 'same deal as before?' text, Bell's 'we'll talk', the unrecorded May 14 call; roughly a coin flip). Given Pinecrest's Oct. 20 posture, the realistic landing zone is $380,000.00-$401,747.50. Pinecrest's Oct. 20 offer (265,200.00 over 6 months, $0 on J-4533, $0 conversion fees, mutual release, each side bears its own fees) is worth about $256,160.04 at the contract's own 1%/month rate ($265,200.00 / 6 = $44,200.00/month; 6-month annuity factor at 1%/month = 5.795476; $44,200.00 x 5.795476 = $256,160.04) - $121,587.46 below even the record floor. It silently drops the $8,847.50 accrued interest, all $71,700.00 of J-4533 (their only particularized defect, ever, is the $3,100.00 we already credited; their audit notice came months after the Section 2 15-day window), the $32,000.00 Anne/Victor fees that have no waiver evidence in any direction, and C.3 - our only fee-shifting provision. Reject as framed; counter at the corridor (see term_sheet.md). Walk-away $377,747.50: below it Pinecrest takes written-conceded or fully documented money, and the arbitration alternative dominates. Projected award (hearing approx. Oct. 2027) gross approx. $421,883.50 = $265,200.00 + $43,323.50 interest through Oct. 31, 2027 (J-4411 18 x $684.00 = $12,312.00; J-4452 17 x $712.50 = $12,112.50; J-4490 16 x $661.00 = $10,576.00; J-4571 14 x $594.50 = $8,323.00) + $57,360.00 J-4533 at an estimated 80% recovery + $56,000.00 fee EV ($32,000.00 + 50% x $48,000.00). Net of C.3 recovery at 60-100% of a $115,000.00-$195,000.00 cost band, arbitration nets approx. $359,883.50 (60% recovery, high cost) to $421,883.50 (full recovery) - C.3 is enforceable as written (Zuniga, in library) and their written 'undisputed' concession makes us the likely prevailing party on the core. The 80% and 50% figures are estimates, labeled as such. Candid caveat: if C.3 recovery comes in under 50%, accepting a lump sum in the $345,747.50-$377,747.50 band could still be rational - that is a client risk call, not something the record compels. fee_exposure_if_arbitrated = $195,000.00: the top of our all-in planning band $115,000.00-$195,000.00 (250-400 attorney hours x $400.00/hr = $100,000.00-$160,000.00, plus AAA filing/arbitrator/administration $15,000.00-$35,000.00). PLANNING PLACEHOLDERS - no AAA fee schedule exists in the library; verify against the current AAA Commercial Rules fee schedule before quoting the client. C.3 cuts both ways: recoverable if we substantially prevail; the filing-mistake scenario (our own motion-to-compel loss or a court complaint) would add their motion fees (est. $15,000.00-$40,000.00, also placeholder). Their Oct. 20 threat to seek C.3 fees 'if you push the interference claim in arbitration' costs us $0: the tort theory is abandoned and will not be re-asserted in any forum, per the session-2 reply letter and advice.",
  "fee_exposure_if_arbitrated": 195000.00
}

